{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sonification sonification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md","fileName":"Sonification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sonification","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[XR Display Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Display Systems","Auditory Display","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sonification sonification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md","fileName":"Sonification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sonification","heading":"Sonification","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Sonification is the process of turning information into sound. It is the auditory counterpart of visualizing data.\n\nA mapping assigns data properties to audible properties such as pitch, intensity, timing, or spatial location. For example, moving a hand through a fluid-flow dataset could produce sounds whose frequencies vary with flow speed. This lets an [[Auditory Display]] communicate patterns without requiring continuous visual attention.\n\nThe mapping must remain understandable and should complement rather than overload other information channels.","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Display Systems","Auditory Display","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sonification sonification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sonification.md","fileName":"Sonif